# Confidentiality survival — by agreement

> Module Confidentiality_duration

Sources: SYN-001 § 11.2 (Acme/Northwind MSA, three years) and SYN-011 § 4.2 (Acme/Vertex
NDA, five years). The two periods differ but do **not** conflict: the agreement is an input
to the scope, so each definition governs its own agreement. This is the calibration case
from `gold/conflicts.jsonl` (CONF-012) in executable form.

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration Agreement:
  -- NorthwindMsa
  -- VertexNda

declaration scope ConfidentialityDuration:
  input disclosure_date content date
  input agreement content Agreement
  input is_trade_secret content boolean

  output obligation_end content date
  output indefinite content boolean
```

## SYN-001 § 11.2 — three years, and trade secrets for as long as they are secret

  The obligations in Section 11.1 continue for three (3) years after the date of
  disclosure, except that obligations with respect to information that qualifies as a
  trade secret continue for as long as the information remains a trade secret.

```catala
scope ConfidentialityDuration:
  label msa_11_2
  definition obligation_end equals disclosure_date + 3 year

  definition indefinite equals is_trade_secret
```

## SYN-011 § 4.2 — five years under the Vertex NDA

  The obligations in Section 3 continue for five (5) years after the date of each
  disclosure. Obligations with respect to information that constitutes a trade secret
  continue for so long as the information remains a trade secret under applicable law.

```catala
scope ConfidentialityDuration:
  exception msa_11_2
  definition obligation_end
    under condition agreement = Agreement.VertexNda
    consequence equals disclosure_date + 5 year
```
